.TH VPN-MANAGER 1 "2026-11-21" "VPN Manager 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vpn-manager \- manage WireGuard tunnels for the current user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vpn-manager
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B VPN Manager
is a desktop client for WireGuard. It lists the profiles under the operator's
configuration directory and the WireGuard connections NetworkManager owns,
imports and exports profiles, connects and disconnects through NetworkManager,
and shows the live state, the transfer counters, the IPv6 classification and the
DNS containment.
.PP
Everything happens in the operator's own configuration directory. The
application never elevates, never runs a privileged helper, and never reads or
writes
.IR /etc/wireguard .
.PP
Only one instance runs per user: starting the application again surfaces the
window of the running instance and the new process exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config\-dir " " \fIpath\fR
Manage the profile files in
.I path
instead of the default directory.
.TP
.B \-\-read\-only
Browse and export without changing anything.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics
Print what is readable without a display and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run the display-free self-test and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage text and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vpnmanager/vpn-manager
The per-user profile directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/vpnmanager/vpn-manager
The application state, its log, its operation journal and its crash log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR wg (8),
.BR wg-quick (8)
